llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: after a commute the two-address pass tests the operand tied before it, as 3.7 (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION in TwoAddressInstructionPass's
tryInstructionTransform. r249378 (Craig Topper, llvm-project 2c4068f40966,
2015-10-06, "[TwoAddressInstructionPass] When looking for a 3 addr
conversion after commuting, make sure regB has been updated to take into
account the commute", first release LLVM 3.8) re-samples regB and its
kill state after a commute; 3.7 does not, so its three-address conversion
sees the operand that was tied before the commute (live through, so not
killed) and turns the commuted `add` into a `lea`. 0xcef1b0 and 0x1393620
are equal to the base in the prebuilt 3.7.1's module and lost in 3.8.1's;
the first pass that differs is this one and nothing before it (round
216B). The one matched row that had needed r249378, 0xbe5650, was 3.7.1's
own miss as the tree wrote it; written as the block's relative offsets
are read (each offset added to the block's address as an integer, offset
first) it is equal under 3.7.1, 3.8.1 and this line with or without the
patch, and the tree has that form from this commit. With the patch
0xcef1b0 and 0x1393620 compile to the base's bytes, 0xeaaec0 goes from 15
to 18 of 20, fifteen functions of the module change and no other matched
game row changes (round 216B, which built and swept this unconditional
form alone).

diff -ru a/lib/CodeGen/TwoAddressInstructionPass.cpp b/lib/CodeGen/TwoAddressInstructionPass.cpp
--- a/lib/CodeGen/TwoAddressInstructionPass.cpp
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/TwoAddressInstructionPass.cpp
@@ -1263,12 +1263,9 @@
     return true;
   }
 
-  // If we commuted, regB may have changed so we should re-sample it to avoid
-  // confusing the three address conversion below.
-  if (Commuted) {
-    regB = MI.getOperand(SrcIdx).getReg();
-    regBKilled = isKilled(MI, regB, MRI, TII, LIS, true);
-  }
+  // PS4: regB and regBKilled are not re-sampled after a commute (the three
+  // address conversion below sees the operand tied before the commute), as
+  // before r249378 (2c4068f40966, first in 3.8): not taken.
 
   if (MI.isConvertibleTo3Addr()) {
     // This instruction is potentially convertible to a true
